# Document descriptions (Elementplan)

Write `description` so an LLM can check whether a file fits the document type. Keep `definition` as the short catalog purpose.

## Template

```yaml
description:
  de: |-
    - {required content 1}
    - {required content 2}
    - {required content 3}
    - {required content 4}
  fr: |-
    - {required content 1}
    - {required content 2}
    - {required content 3}
    - {required content 4}
  it: |-
    - {required content 1}
    - {required content 2}
    - {required content 3}
    - {required content 4}
  en: |-
    - {required content 1}
    - {required content 2}
    - {required content 3}
    - {required content 4}
```

Place `description` after `definition`, before `file_name`.

## Rules

1. **Checkable contents only**: 4–6 bullets of what must be observable on the file (drawing, report, table, contract).
2. No section headers. No “what it is not”.
3. No `Ifc*` tokens. Construction language.
4. Do not restate `name` or copy `definition`.
5. All four languages: same bullets and meaning in `de`, `fr`, `it`, `en`.
6. **Write from German, not from English word order.** Default language is `de`. FR/IT must sound like Swiss planning language, not like a calque of EN.

## Tone / calques (do not use)

| Concept | de | fr (native) | it (native) | avoid |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| keep in model | im Modell führen | saisir / tenir dans la maquette | gestire / tenere nel modello | FR *Porter* |
| derive | ableiten / berechnen | déduire / calculer / obtenir | ricavare / calcolare | FR *dériver*, IT *Derivare* |
| MEP medium | Medium | fluide | fluido | FR *médium*, IT *mezzo* (unless “by means of”) |
| component | Bauteil | élément | componente | FR *composant* as default |
| MEP | TGA | CVC | impianti | TGA in FR/IT; FR *GT* |
| title block | Plankopf | cartouche | cartiglio | |
| scale | Massstab | échelle | scala | |
| storey | Geschoss | étage | piano | |
| tenant placeholder | `{Mietername}` | `{nom du locataire}` | `{nome locatario}` | German token in FR/IT |

Do not translate IFC/property tokens.
